e  and then the bishop take here on g7  attacking the rook  and this is where there's not a lot of  great options here you could  play something like d6 okay well  just trying to open up the door for the  light square bishop to get involved  but then the bishop just takes here on  h8 that doesn't feel really good  they could always get their queen so  maybe queen to  g4 and then after we take here on h8  which they cannot stop  then they take here on e4  check but then queen to e2  attacking the queen says yeah if you  want to trade off that's fine we're just  up so much material and also if they  move their queen  they have to be cautious because queen  to e8  would be checkmate if they move their  queen to the wrong spot so  in many cases they almost have to take  here but after the king takes  you can see they're they're in a pretty  tough spot they need to move their  knight they don't want to move it to f6  because that would just fall to the  bishop here  on h8 so they're looking at knight to e7  and then knight to  c3 but if you look at the material white  is up a minor piece  and a rook that's not going to be good  they have a pass pawn here on the f-file  there's no way black should even be in  this game  and white should have a pretty easy end  game from here so that is the danish  bird trap  with the few variations that you could  potentially see if they don't fall for  it completely  either way white's definitely going to  have a good game so if your opponent  ever plays  queen 2 g5 in the danish gambit you  should uh your eyes should light up  and just hope that after you played  knight to f3  that they come down and take here and  take the bait for the trap here on  g2 hopefully you guys enjoyed this video  thanks for all the support of the  channel if you have any suggestions for  future videos  please let me know in the comments below  or you can always email me as well at  the test website at  gmail.com but thanks so much and i'll  see you guys in  